= Emergence =
Emergence describes system-level properties, patterns, or behaviors that arise from interactions among components and are not usefully characterized by examining isolated components alone.

== Overview ==
Emergence does not imply that higher-level behavior is uncaused or supernatural. It describes the explanatory importance of organization, interaction, scale, and collective dynamics.

== Examples ==
Common examples include collective behavior in social insects, pattern formation, market dynamics, neural population activity, ecological organization, and macroscopic properties arising from microscopic interactions.

